# The extractor's local development environment (services/extractor/.venv):
# the runtime and fixture-generator dependencies, plus the development tools
# (prompt 3 section 12). This is the input. The installable file is
# requirements-dev.lock, compiled from it with every transitive dependency pinned
# and hashed, constrained by the two other locks so that every shared dependency
# keeps one version. After changing a pin here or in the other .in files,
# regenerate the locks in order (requirements.lock, requirements-fixtures.lock,
# requirements-dev.lock) as docs/adr/0001-toolchain-and-monorepo.md and
# docs/adr/0018-extractor-dependencies-and-sandbox-image.md describe, and install
# only from the lock, with --require-hashes (pnpm setup:py).
-c requirements.lock
-c requirements-fixtures.lock
-r requirements.in
-r requirements-fixtures.in

